---
// One-page portfolio. Static, no client-side JS.
import "@fontsource-variable/inter";

const title = "Yuliia Erdyv · Revenue Operations";
const description =
  "Revenue operations analyst in Charlotte, NC. Daily revenue reporting, forecasting, and sales coaching analytics built on Snowflake SQL and self-contained HTML dashboards.";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark" />
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:title" content={title} />
    <meta property="og:description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <title>{title}</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <nav aria-label="Sections">
      <a href="#work">Work</a>
      <a href="#experience">Experience</a>
      <a href="#education">Education</a>
      <a href="/resume.pdf">Resume</a>
      <a href="#contact">Contact</a>
    </nav>
    <main>
      <header class="hero">
        <img class="portrait" src="/img/yuliia.jpg" width="480" height="480" alt="Portrait of Yuliia Erdyv" />
        <p class="kicker">Charlotte, NC · Revenue Operations</p>
        <h1>Yuliia Erdyv</h1>
        <p class="tagline">
          I build the reports sales leaders run their day on: daily revenue
          and funnel reporting, forecasting, and rep-level coaching analytics.
        </p>
        <p class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button" href="#work">See the work</a>
          <a class="button ghost" href="/resume.pdf">Resume (PDF)</a>
          <a class="button ghost" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/erdyv-yuliia">LinkedIn</a>
          <a class="button ghost" href="https://github.com/AiYulia">GitHub</a>
          <a class="button ghost" href="mailto:erdyv.yuliia@gmail.com">Email</a>
        </p>
      </header>

      <section id="work" aria-labelledby="work-heading">
        <h2 id="work-heading">Work</h2>
        <p class="section-note">
          Two real reports from my Revenue Operations work, published with
          every channel, rep, and director name and every number changed.
          Layout, logic, and calculations are the originals.
        </p>

        <article class="build">
          <a class="shot" href="https://aiyulia.github.io/daily-revenue-report/dashboard.html">
            <img src="/img/daily-revenue-report.png" width="1440" height="900" loading="lazy"
              alt="Daily Revenue Operations dashboard: green header band, grouped tab bar, and trend charts by lead priority" />
          </a>
          <div class="build-head">
            <h3>Daily Revenue Operations</h3>
            <span class="badge">Live</span>
          </div>
          <p class="problem">The sales floor's morning read, in one page.</p>
          <p>
            A daily report rebuilt from an Excel workbook into a single
            self-contained HTML page, in the dashboard style I developed for
            the teams. Funnel trends by lead priority and marketing channel
            (calls per lead, PQL to QL, PQL to enroll, QL to enroll, percent
            reached), 5-day and weekly aggregates, a rep-tier view, enrollment
            mix shift, weekend trends, and the raw data and SQL behind every
            number.
          </p>
          <p class="tags">
            <span>Snowflake SQL</span><span>Python</span><span>self-contained HTML</span><span>SVG charts</span>
          </p>
          <p class="build-actions">
            <a class="button" href="https://aiyulia.github.io/daily-revenue-report/dashboard.html">Open the dashboard</a>
            <a class="button ghost" href="https://github.com/AiYulia/daily-revenue-report">GitHub</a>
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="build">
          <a class="shot" href="https://aiyulia.github.io/directors-workbook/dashboard.html">
            <img src="/img/directors-workbook.png" width="1440" height="900" loading="lazy"
              alt="Director Coaching Workbook: rep leaderboard by team with tier, score, and goal pace" />
          </a>
          <div class="build-head">
            <h3>Director Coaching Workbook</h3>
            <span class="badge">Live</span>
          </div>
          <p class="problem">Which rep needs which coaching, and on which leads.</p>
          <p>
            Sales directors' workbook for tiering and coaching reps: team
            leaderboards, conversion by lead source and channel tier against
            the sales-floor benchmark, dialer activity by hour and day, and the
            conversation-data section I added, which scores call transcripts
            for objection rebuttals, discovery, and talk share against each
            tier's median.
          </p>
          <p class="tags">
            <span>Snowflake SQL</span><span>Python</span><span>call-transcript scoring</span><span>self-contained HTML</span>
          </p>
          <p class="build-actions">
            <a class="button" href="https://aiyulia.github.io/directors-workbook/dashboard.html">Open the workbook</a>
            <a class="button ghost" href="https://github.com/AiYulia/directors-workbook">GitHub</a>
          </p>
        </article>
      </section>

      <section id="experience" aria-labelledby="experience-heading">
        <h2 id="experience-heading">Experience</h2>

        <article class="role">
          <div class="role-head">
            <h3>JG Wentworth</h3>
            <span class="when">Aug 2024 – Sep 2026</span>
          </div>
          <p class="role-title">Revenue Operations Analyst</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Developed the corporate dashboard style adopted by every team while rebuilding Power BI and Excel reports as HTML on shared, Airflow-scheduled Snowflake SQL; helped add an AI summary (RAG) to the morning alert email naming which metrics suffered and why.</li>
            <li>Upgraded the MBR/QBR profitability package for the C-suite and VPs, with a mirrored interactive dashboard that expands every summary figure into its underlying detail.</li>
            <li>Built separate weekday and weekend forecasts with time-series regression and day-of-week seasonality, which surfaced a cheap bucket of Sunday leads worth buying and working first thing Monday.</li>
            <li>Added a conversation-data section to Sales' Directors Workbook, scoring call transcripts for sentiment, objections, and rebuttals; it spotted experienced new hires before any enrollment data existed and cut their onboarding from 3 months to 1.</li>
            <li>Built a marketing-by-sales view in 15-minute cohorts that exposed two timing gaps: evening leads waiting on too few Pacific-time reps, and morning paid-search leads going cold before first contact.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="role">
          <div class="role-head">
            <h3>J.P. Morgan · U.S. Private Bank</h3>
            <span class="when">May 2024 – Aug 2024</span>
          </div>
          <p class="role-title">Summer Analyst, Asset &amp; Wealth Management</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Built a branch-referral tracker in Python, Excel, and VBA for high-net-worth clients walking into Chase branches in five cities, connecting Private Bank bankers with Chase regional directors; it brought in 2 new clients during the internship and stayed in use after it ended.</li>
            <li>Built the cash-redeployment pipeline for every banker and investor on the floor ahead of expected Fed rate cuts, ranking clients by idle cash in Excel (Office Script), with Monte Carlo forecasts for client meetings; it helped move $750M from cash into invested assets.</li>
            <li>Co-built an AI prospect-research app on the ChatGPT API and owned its API integration and source-verification layer; the summer-long project won 1st of 12 eight-person teams.</li>
            <li>Handled client communication for the banker and investor team with market analysis from the Bloomberg Terminal, and kept a weekly report on client activity and outreach progress.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="role">
          <div class="role-head">
            <h3>David W. Chefec</h3>
            <span class="when">Nov 2022 – Apr 2024</span>
          </div>
          <p class="role-title">Legal Assistant Paralegal</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Designed and maintained an Excel case and deadline tracker giving the attorney one up-to-date view of every matter's stage and upcoming filings.</li>
            <li>Drafted filings, forms, and client correspondence, and ran client intake and follow-ups from first contact through final submission.</li>
            <li>Managed billing and collections reporting: invoices, incoming payments, and regular summaries of outstanding balances.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </section>

      <section id="education" aria-labelledby="education-heading">
        <h2 id="education-heading">Education</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>BBA, Business Analytics (STEM), minor in Finance</strong>,
          Hofstra University, May 2025. GPA 4.0 (major) / 3.98 (cumulative),
          Honors College Degree with Distinction, Presidential Scholarship.
          Best Paper, Journal of International Business &amp; Law ("Homes for
          Profit," 2025).
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="skills" aria-labelledby="skills-heading">
        <h2 id="skills-heading">Skills</h2>
        <dl class="skills">
          <dt>Revenue operations</dt>
          <dd>Forecasting, pipeline and funnel analysis, conversion and win-rate analysis, rep-level performance tracking, CRM and pipeline hygiene, staffing and capacity modeling, MBR/QBR reporting, process documentation</dd>
          <dt>Tools</dt>
          <dd>Excel (advanced modeling, scenario analysis, Office Script), Google Sheets, Salesforce, SQL (Snowflake), Tableau, Power BI, Python (pandas), HTML reporting, Five9, Observe.AI</dd>
          <dt>AI</dt>
          <dd>Claude and Claude Code, Snowflake Cortex AI, LLM-based sentiment and semantic scoring, prompt engineering</dd>
        </dl>
      </section>

      <footer class="contact" id="contact">
        <a href="mailto:erdyv.yuliia@gmail.com">erdyv.yuliia@gmail.com</a>
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/erdyv-yuliia">LinkedIn</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/AiYulia">GitHub</a>
        <a href="/resume.pdf">Resume</a>
      </footer>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #faf9f5;
    --surface: #f0eee6;
    --text: #141413;
    --muted: #5f5e57;
    --rule: #ddd8cb;
    --accent: #c15f3c;
    --accent-ink: #a84b2b;
    color-scheme: light dark;
  }

  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root {
      --bg: #1a1915;
      --surface: #232019;
      --text: #edeae3;
      --muted: #a39f93;
      --rule: #35322a;
      --accent: #e08d63;
      --accent-ink: #eda37f;
    }
  }

  * {
    margin: 0;
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  html {
    background: var(--bg);
    scroll-behavior: smooth;
  }

  body {
    font-family: "Inter Variable", -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Helvetica, Arial,
      sans-serif;
    font-feature-settings: "cv11", "ss01";
    color: var(--text);
    line-height: 1.6;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }

  nav {
    max-width: 48rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 1.5rem 1.5rem 0;
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  nav a {
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  nav a:hover,
  nav a:focus-visible {
    color: var(--accent-ink);
  }

  main {
    max-width: 48rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 4.5rem 1.5rem 5rem;
    animation: fade-in 0.6s ease-out both;
  }

  @keyframes fade-in {
    from {
      opacity: 0;
      transform: translateY(6px);
    }
    to {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: none;
    }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    main {
      animation: none;
    }
    html {
      scroll-behavior: auto;
    }
  }

  .hero {
    margin-bottom: 4rem;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
    column-gap: 2.5rem;
  }

  .hero > * {
    grid-column: 1;
  }

  .hero > .portrait {
    grid-column: 2;
    grid-row: 1 / span 4;
    align-self: start;
    width: 168px;
    height: 168px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    object-fit: cover;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    margin-top: 0.25rem;
  }

  .kicker {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent-ink);
    margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 6.5vw, 3.5rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    line-height: 1.05;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .tagline {
    font-size: clamp(1.12rem, 2.6vw, 1.3rem);
    font-weight: 450;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    line-height: 1.5;
    max-width: 40rem;
  }

  .subline {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 1rem;
    max-width: 38rem;
  }

  .hero-actions {
    margin-top: 1.9rem;
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.65rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .button {
    display: inline-block;
    background: var(--accent);
    color: var(--bg);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    padding: 0.55rem 1.15rem;
    border-radius: 8px;
    border: 1px solid transparent;
  }

  .button:hover,
  .button:focus-visible {
    text-decoration: none;
    filter: brightness(1.07);
  }

  .button.ghost {
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--accent-ink);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .button.ghost:hover,
  .button.ghost:focus-visible {
    border-color: var(--accent);
    filter: none;
  }

  section {
    margin-bottom: 4.5rem;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 650;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding-top: 1.6rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.6rem;
  }

  .section-note {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    max-width: 40rem;
  }

  .build {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 14px;
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .shot {
    display: block;
    margin: 0 0 1.2rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 8px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: #fff;
  }

  .shot img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  .build-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.7rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
  }

  .badge {
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 650;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--bg);
    background: var(--accent);
    padding: 0.12rem 0.55rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  h3 {
    font-size: 1.22rem;
    font-weight: 650;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
  }

  .problem {
    font-weight: 550;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 0.55rem;
  }

  .build p {
    margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
    font-size: 0.96rem;
  }

  .build p:not(.problem):not(.tags):not(.build-actions) {
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.05rem;
  }

  .tags span {
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    font-weight: 550;
    color: var(--muted);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 0.08rem 0.5rem;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .build-actions {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-bottom: 0 !important;
  }

  .build-actions .button {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    padding: 0.45rem 1rem;
  }

  .role {
    padding: 1.3rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .role:first-of-type {
    padding-top: 0;
  }

  .role:last-of-type {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .role-head {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .role h3 {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.1rem;
  }

  .when {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .role-title {
    color: var(--accent-ink);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 0.55rem;
  }

  .role ul {
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .role li {
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }

  .role li::marker {
    color: var(--rule);
  }

  #education p {
    max-width: 42rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  #education strong {
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .skills {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 11rem 1fr;
    gap: 0.6rem 1.25rem;
    font-size: 0.94rem;
  }

  .skills dt {
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .skills dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  a {
    color: var(--accent-ink);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  a:hover,
  a:focus-visible {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .contact {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    margin-top: 3.5rem;
    padding-top: 1.75rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem 2rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    main {
      padding-top: 3rem;
    }
    .hero {
      margin-bottom: 3rem;
      display: block;
    }
    .hero > .portrait {
      display: block;
      width: 104px;
      height: 104px;
      margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    }
    section {
      margin-bottom: 3.5rem;
    }
    .build {
      padding: 1rem 1rem 1.25rem;
    }
    nav {
      gap: 1rem;
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
    }
    .role-head {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0;
    }
    .skills {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.2rem;
    }
    .skills dd {
      margin-bottom: 0.7rem;
    }
  }
</style>
